  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc while image (resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 20.8% acc, making RNA the clearly dominant modality. However, we have only one RNA encoder tested (linear PCA). Question: Does a learned, biologically-informed RNA representation (scvi_n200) outperform linear PCA in capturing task-relevant structure? This is a clean single-variable change from config_001 (same model_setting, same profile_setting, only encoder differs), isolating the RNA encoder effect. Why best next experiment: Since RNA is the stronger modality, improving its representation has the highest expected payoff. If scvi_n200 improves over PCA, it validates learned representations and makes the many multimodal scvi configurations (config_028-039) high-value follow-ups. If it does not improve, PCA is sufficient and we can redirect budget toward multiprofile/aggregation or fusion design. This single experiment reduces the largest current uncertainty about the most impactful design axis."
